a3a7e7049d2a55f","node_id":"C_kwDOHRI_RdoAKDNlOTY0MThlOTliMTIwOTZkN2M1NzA5ZTBhM2E3ZTcwNDlkMmE1NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commit/64a98858568c9e56dc507b8a24cccc8c81cfbc4d","sha":"64a98858568c9e56dc507b8a24cccc8c81cfbc4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/64a98858568c9e56dc507b8a24cccc8c81cfbc4d"}],"sha":"3e96418e99b12096d7c5709e0a3a7e7049d2a55f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/3e96418e99b12096d7c5709e0a3a7e7049d2a55f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97442151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shmufeld","id":97442151,"login":"shmufeld","node_id":"U_kgDOBc7ZZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/64a98858568c9e56dc507b8a24cccc8c81cfbc4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T11:53:19Z","email":"97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com","name":"shmufeld"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T11:53:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"state-mirror (4/4): runtime + health (#378)\n\n* state-mirror (4/4): runtime loop, restore entrypoint, health/metrics\n\nFinal slice of the StateMirror sidecar (stacked on PR 3/4); completes the\ncomponent so the image is functional.\n\n- mirror: the long-running sidecar loop -- watch (debounced) + periodic full\n  scan, observed-delete reconcile (bounded, O(1) drop-oldest), unobserved\n  drift kept-and-counted (backend wins on ambiguity), liveness heartbeat inside\n  the scan/drain loops so a slow backend can''t trip the probe and lose the\n  emptyDir.\n- restore: the one-shot init-container entrypoint (fail-closed).\n- watcher: watchdog-based filesystem event handler + path resolution.\n- health: readiness/liveness HTTP server and the Prometheus metric surface\n  (backend-neutral names matching the chart''s cross-repo contract).\n\nAfter this PR the tree equals the original #373 branch.\nTests: full suite (mirror, watcher, health) green; ruff clean.\n\n* state-mirror (4/4): address PR #378 review (honor observed moves + metrics/typing polish)\n\n- watcher: on EVENT_MOVED, also queue a delete for the OLD path when it was a\n  tracked entry (a renamed single file, or a child inside a watched dir) so a\n  later restore does not revive the file at its old location. Consistent with\n  how EVENT_DELETED is already handled, and safe against atomic\n  write-temp-then-rename: the drain only deletes when the source path is gone\n  and store.delete is idempotent. (@vg12345)\n- health: snapshot() now excludes private attrs (the lock) so it is a clean\n  data-only dict; render_metrics derives state_mirror_ready from that same\n  snapshot instead of a second is_ready() lock (one consistent scrape).\n- restore.run(): annotate the store parameter as Store.\n- mirror.run_forever(): document the scan/poll interval defaults.\n- build_observer: log when a missing watch directory is created.\n\nLeft out: the \"global log\" rebinding (a no-op -- setup_logging returns the same\ngetLogger singleton) and dropping poll_sqlite''s isinstance guard (it provides\ntype narrowing / defensive depth).\n\nTests: +2 move-cleanup regression tests; 172 pass, ruff check + format clean.","tree":{"sha":"3e642c4a60e1c7dfddb6179c7a828688b2c511d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/3e642c4a60e1c7dfddb6179c7a828688b2c511d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/64a98858568c9e56dc507b8a24cccc8c81cfbc4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e642c4a60e1c7dfddb6179c7a828688b2c511d8\nparent 7b5f4b9cc2daecdcaf1d4ee17b4090481af5288a\nauthor shmufeld <97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com> 1782388399 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782388399 +0300\n\nstate-mirror (4/4): runtime + health (#378)\n\n* state-mirror (4/4): runtime loop, restore entrypoint, health/metrics\n\nFinal slice of the StateMirror sidecar (stacked on PR 3/4); completes the\ncomponent so the image is functional.\n\n- mirror: the long-running sidecar loop -- watch (debounced) + periodic full\n  scan, observed-delete reconcile (bounded, O(1) drop-oldest), unobserved\n  drift kept-and-counted (backend wins on ambiguity), liveness heartbeat inside\n  the scan/drain loops so a slow backend can''t trip the probe and lose the\n  emptyDir.\n- restore: the one-shot init-container entrypoint (fail-closed).\n- watcher: watchdog-based filesystem event handler + path resolution.\n- health: readiness/liveness HTTP server and the Prometheus metric surface\n  (backend-neutral names matching the chart''s cross-repo contract).\n\nAfter this PR the tree equals the original #373 branch.\nTests: full suite (mirror, watcher, health) green; ruff clean.\n\n* state-mirror (4/4): address PR #378 review (honor observed moves + metrics/typing polish)\n\n- watcher: on EVENT_MOVED, also queue a delete for the OLD path when it was a\n  tracked entry (a renamed single file, or a child inside a watched dir) so a\n  later restore does not revive the file at its old location. Consistent with\n  how EVENT_DELETED is already handled, and safe against atomic\n  write-temp-then-rename: the drain only deletes when the source path is gone\n  and store.delete is idempotent. (@vg12345)\n- health: snapshot() now excludes private attrs (the lock) so it is a clean\n  data-only dict; render_metrics derives state_mirror_ready from that same\n  snapshot instead of a second is_ready() lock (one consistent scrape).\n- restore.run(): annotate the store parameter as Store.\n- mirror.run_forever(): document the scan/poll interval defaults.\n- build_observer: log when a missing watch directory is created.\n\nLeft out: the \"global log\" rebinding (a no-op -- setup_logging returns the same\ngetLogger singleton) and dropping poll_sqlite''s isinstance guard (it provides\ntype narrowing / defensive depth).\n\nTests: +2 move-cleanup regression tests; 172 pass, ruff check + format clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPRavCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+0IQAE23sPmGIU5ONsH5k31SQVjX\nsPcwB7w018cuBZZhHV2Bu/+16hO15JRBLZOlUMcMQMlKst/4o3jGSN1QKdwkne2m\ndLum0IYJ/lQ2bGIDKJKh4GaHkf33kW2s1lycwYxAmqUBByBM/9INoGoU8ITPSvst\nTyUMtByAjgETZxYPLmcrI8hMMSwBeimhpdqp8pUBq1GGR3tSZAhMYRWdJZdsKj5U\nX+Xbdgoq31L8pn4t85QTju0Hw3BQALzeJNHWBWZMjpp8mxqYiw3GodKWvZjrR5bL\n0BL0EWX9n8JQVwlb2rbg73QrghIBLJ6VmI6LDA0CPPBYQwvi61/NssqARzLeI61z\nq4ivgqapqSJu35D+s16qfVu23u4U2SemMhNP5eGyXquhQkONwY1YAX3a0TTRtT1j\ngNmN248i41ceMNaZo/wAFgI/zBBllUQR5U92qJx1xEyIRM8fcrb2z+R1jWud7vr0\nli/sldpUVsAWHwHEH5RL67uAWbIj/o9YVui0wKnfhwGePRpCe5+QyPYnVbvj59Re\nc1Ii/FcZj6AOigIqjizMO0L2XWwg1iumrtfIdxPj4+X83ysuQ/flSrbwRjQyZbjc\nZqKlqPb7YbO5Yt4QlCJucU8C1IqrYurOJXFRYgo+XHr16SDJlatUA0cc/zObhpF+\nKR79a1Zz81l7LoPUBw8Y\n=G4jl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-25T11:53:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists