"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/7b5f4b9cc2daecdcaf1d4ee17b4090481af5288a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T10:03:09Z","email":"97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com","name":"shmufeld"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T10:03:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"state-mirror (3/4): handlers + routing (#377)\n\n* state-mirror (3/4): file-type handlers + backend routing\n\nThird slice of the StateMirror sidecar (stacked on PR 2/4).\n\nAdds the per-file-type mirror/restore logic and the wiring that binds it to a\nbackend:\n- handlers: BaseHandler plus blob, atomic_blob, directory (per-child keys,\n  realpath-containment guard on restore) and sqlite (consistent online-backup\n  snapshot, WAL-aware change signature, fail-closed integrity check on\n  restore). _write_file preserves the destination''s uid/gid/mode across the\n  tmp+rename so a root-run restore does not strip ownership.\n- backends: install-wide backend selection (STATE_MIRROR_BACKEND) building a\n  single Store at startup and binding each classifier entry''s handler to it.\n\nThe mirror/restore entrypoints and health/metrics server follow in PR 4/4.\nTests: handlers, sqlite, backend routing; ruff clean.\n\n* state-mirror (3/4): address PR #377 review (fail-closed restore, honest backend errors)\n\n- sqlite restore: integrity-check the stored snapshot on a throwaway temp copy\n  *before* touching the live DB, then write through the ownership-preserving\n  _write_file. A corrupt backend object now fails closed without destroying the\n  installer-seeded DB (and without re-introducing the root-owns-gv.db\n  regression a raw os.replace would cause). (@vg12345)\n- directory mirror: stop swallowing backend errors. Only a local OSError on a\n  child read is skipped; a WireError propagates so the loop records the outage\n  via record_store_down instead of reporting a healthy run during a partition.\n  (@vg12345)\n- base.on_delete: document that deletes are not durable across a restore for\n  baseline=image/empty entries (the file is re-seeded) -- \"backend wins\";\n  durable deletes would need a tombstone (future work). (@vg12345)\n- directory scan: os.scandir instead of listdir+isfile (one stat per entry);\n  follow_symlinks=True preserves the prior os.path.isfile semantics.\n\nTests: +3 regression tests (live DB survives a corrupt snapshot; directory\nmirror propagates a backend error; unreadable child is skipped). 127 pass,\nruff check clean.","tree":{"sha":"40b21bd5c5519470dbcb58fcf2892a56a3cb643b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/40b21bd5c5519470dbcb58fcf2892a56a3cb643b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/7b5f4b9cc2daecdcaf1d4ee17b4090481af5288a","verification":{"payload":"tree 40b21bd5c5519470dbcb58fcf2892a56a3cb643b\nparent 793b88500eb05d392d056f772eb786ae4eb643e1\nauthor shmufeld <97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com> 1782381789 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782381789 +0300\n\nstate-mirror (3/4): handlers + routing (#377)\n\n* state-mirror (3/4): file-type handlers + backend routing\n\nThird slice of the StateMirror sidecar (stacked on PR 2/4).\n\nAdds the per-file-type mirror/restore logic and the wiring that binds it to a\nbackend:\n- handlers: BaseHandler plus blob, atomic_blob, directory (per-child keys,\n  realpath-containment guard on restore) and sqlite (consistent online-backup\n  snapshot, WAL-aware change signature, fail-closed integrity check on\n  restore). _write_file preserves the destination''s uid/gid/mode across the\n  tmp+rename so a root-run restore does not strip ownership.\n- backends: install-wide backend selection (STATE_MIRROR_BACKEND) building a\n  single Store at startup and binding each classifier entry''s handler to it.\n\nThe mirror/restore entrypoints and health/metrics server follow in PR 4/4.\nTests: handlers, sqlite, backend routing; ruff clean.\n\n* state-mirror (3/4): address PR #377 review (fail-closed restore, honest backend errors)\n\n- sqlite restore: integrity-check the stored snapshot on a throwaway temp copy\n  *before* touching the live DB, then write through the ownership-preserving\n  _write_file. A corrupt backend object now fails closed without destroying the\n  installer-seeded DB (and without re-introducing the root-owns-gv.db\n  regression a raw os.replace would cause). (@vg12345)\n- directory mirror: stop swallowing backend errors. Only a local OSError on a\n  child read is skipped; a WireError propagates so the loop records the outage\n  via record_store_down instead of reporting a healthy run during a partition.\n  (@vg12345)\n- base.on_delete: document that deletes are not durable across a restore for\n  baseline=image/empty entries (the file is re-seeded) -- \"backend wins\";\n  durable deletes would need a tombstone (future work). (@vg12345)\n- directory scan: os.scandir instead of listdir+isfile (one stat per entry);\n  follow_symlinks=True preserves the prior os.path.isfile semantics.\n\nTests: +3 regression tests (live DB survives a corrupt snapshot; directory\nmirror propagates a backend error; unreadable child is skipped). 127 pass,\nruff check clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPzdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGyQQAJ99IMn9Prc3MKlBaXvmPl67\nUrs40AZsCmdIYkxBH6MeRqvJ6UxVug064UBQt2Ctc0QZfPyjJQDUFp4cLo7VMkum\nNEhMKcyisLUpzaecsnRShzen9hle2TO70Z/js1rfLnf7JjfthkANKQ27KP4m+VdZ\nTMn4sueQ8bs1kYGCu9NydddE444GI48IPOL4GwM4SnJOmfC4F/wAJIfykLLr2hEN\nisRn0vrnxUBH1sDK1I+g1Rtw3icd0DN6y/HmoxsgS23h2jVFxVVvl+UDgAc7aEk0\ndJJQ2bAUofLEQGfPfD5hVSjygsmEqVAOolVYZsL411yFj9mamsH4OYAIhG0u2ait\neS9+alBXouKoWu8HAASwr9C7UazDStkzXbhFmV89UjkV9t9qNsbr+SAUEUdsKUu1\nQJFD1r0mdIWk7ljckdIe1uyeqlc46Wb6XlA1/QnqdBKXCnqO8BG5aiIlKJvBjqyk\n3zW6v99Z3