privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shmufeld","id":97442151,"login":"shmufeld","node_id":"U_kgDOBc7ZZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/793b88500eb05d392d056f772eb786ae4eb643e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:19:05Z","email":"97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com","name":"shmufeld"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:19:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"state-mirror (2/4): storage backends + clients (#376)\n\nSecond slice of the StateMirror sidecar (stacked on PR 1/4).\n\nAdds the backend-neutral persistence layer:\n- store: the Store port plus RedisStore and ConfigMapStore (one ConfigMap per\n  key, binaryData body + meta field, fail-closed ~1 MiB ceiling, shared\n  wire.verify_body integrity check).\n- redis_client / k8s_client: lazy connection adapters (kubernetes and redis\n  imported lazily so a deployment using only one backend needs only its deps).\n\nHandlers and the routing that picks a backend follow in PR 3/4.\nTests: ConfigMapStore covered; ruff clean.","tree":{"sha":"542f9a87f265ba397c5fc94e6bcde683f1a564d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/542f9a87f265ba397c5fc94e6bcde683f1a564d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/793b88500eb05d392d056f772eb786ae4eb643e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 542f9a87f265ba397c5fc94e6bcde683f1a564d8\nparent ed812945174bede360c186a7a3fff8131dbab429\nauthor shmufeld <97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com> 1782379145 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782379145 +0300\n\nstate-mirror (2/4): storage backends + clients (#376)\n\nSecond slice of the StateMirror sidecar (stacked on PR 1/4).\n\nAdds the backend-neutral persistence layer:\n- store: the Store port plus RedisStore and ConfigMapStore (one ConfigMap per\n  key, binaryData body + meta field, fail-closed ~1 MiB ceiling, shared\n  wire.verify_body integrity check).\n- redis_client / k8s_client: lazy connection adapters (kubernetes and redis\n  imported lazily so a deployment using only one backend needs only its deps).\n\nHandlers and the routing that picks a backend follow in PR 3/4.\nTests: ConfigMapStore covered; ruff clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPKJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAP0QAEUpGKFVS9TuZxRh14yzY+4y\nsnf2zxLfEEcDXViDkuLXEV1t/2xteVJdZAG+HDUslXbMTA851rj8x9EuaAix1GP2\nWsNp7avEk2Y6LOgVez0UwErR3qMuZnRvdWE2pXZbRNMnDe+dSiZMwoUcVbp2Lal0\nH1aG37dwTIYbeisLdSz82GofobP/wi4fMGkmLFM3GrAo3zdsAB07hLq4NpfzAI0O\nWaA4G/cRXJklzQQkxU4T6BIe+/cmWJ38BoH4L9yU9o1O0SERmfyUPef6jrxUli4o\nZK8+dDrYGX4Xf9OoHZ1+BzSz6Epj9v1RTEP4bCuyGXrOsTggCrsQInv7dUUqqVLA\nZR4mVjK8uj+w/ykVAHsP3l6UxcuK5mfU9otxFyCObhWpSwpyPdPyUa7Khci6xmvX\nG15+/RnKloqjsisz9F+ZmkZURatgfXO2QznaEPFmIgUgWS/tvjSrHQTDf5NqdP4Z\n1+UePyhl3pzkkSwao2Gpld6W5ugldD3TErp6CtEm07osVnpPugm7HcWDtQvAMxTC\n46ckqeVCQrveFo6nX52JpN84rdETgRiaHoD+D1ACE+uN3pmwojpM1ALSbkVrMEok\nbSXQzA1tT8fA7OePe9e9JlmgvP7+wx/Jpf1fsBQ9AEnDT60m8do7WXJUwdgmYBZD\nW1icgznVDDUVcIfC4TRz\n=d2uZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-25T09:19:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commit/793b88500eb05d392d056f772eb786ae4eb643e1","node_id":"C_kwDOHRI_RdoAKDc5M2I4ODUwMGViMDVkMzkyZDA1NmY3NzJlYjc4NmFlNGViNjQzZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commit/ed812945174bede360c186a7a3fff8131dbab429","sha":"ed812945174bede360c186a7a3fff8131dbab429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/ed812945174bede360c186a7a3fff8131dbab429"}],"sha":"793b88500eb05d392d056f772eb786ae4eb643e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/793b88500eb05d392d056f772eb786ae4eb643e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97442151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shmufeld","id":97442151,"login":"shmufeld","node_id":"U_kgDOBc7ZZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/ed812945174bede360c186a7a3fff8131dbab429/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T07:19:13Z","email":"97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com","name":"shmufeld"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T07:19:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"state-mirror (1/4): scaffold + foundations (#375)\n\n* state-mirror (1/4): component scaffold + foundation modules\n\nFirst slice of the StateMirror sidecar, split out of #373 for reviewability.\nNet-new, consumer-agnostic component under ufm-state-mirror/.\n\nThis PR lands the packaging/CI/docs scaffold and the dependency-free\nfoundation modules only:\n- packaging: VERSION, build/Dockerfile, build/docker_build.sh, .dockerignore,\n  pyproject (ruff/pytest config), requirements, BUILD.md, README, and the\n  example classifier.\n- CI: .github/workflows/state-mirror-ci.yml (ruff + pytest + docker build,\n  scoped to ufm-state-mirror/**).\n- engine foundations: wire (on-the-wire body+meta + integrity verify),\n  classifier (YAML schema/validation), redis_errors / k8s_errors (reason\n  taxonomies), logconfig.\n\nStorage backends, handlers, and the runtime loop follow in PRs 2-4.\nTests for these modules pass; ruff clean.\n\n* state-mirror (1/4): address review feedback\n\n- classifier: strict boolean coercion for `recursive` (a quoted \"false\" no\n  longer becomes True); reject duplicate/nested keyspaces (a redis_key under a\n  directory redis_key_prefix, or nested prefixes) and report all uniqueness\n  problems in one aggregated error instead of failing on the first; move the\n  PyYAML import to the module head.\n- redis_errors: classify redis-py exception classes via a name->reason map\n  walked over the MRO (subclass wins over base) instead of an if-chain.\n- wire / logconfig: clearer variable names (d->data, root->root_logger).\n- example classifier: note it is illustrative, not the authoritative file set\n  (which ships in the consumer repo).\n- tests: cover strict bool, keyspace overlap/nesting, and aggregated errors.\n\n* ufm-state-mirror/state_mirror/classifier.py\n\nformatting\n\n* formatting\n\n* state-mirror (1/4): address PR #375 review feedback\n\n- wire: check `body is None` before the format-version guard in verify_body so\n  a missing body reports the correct error; keep the pre-fetch format guard in\n  read_and_verify via a shared _ensure_supported_format() helper (so a too-new\n  format is still refused without fetching a possibly large body). Adds\n  regression tests for both paths.\n- wire: document the distinct roles of Meta.format_version (wire layout,\n  enforced on read) vs schema_version (reserved content-schema marker).\n- Dockerfile: justify the python:3.12-slim (Debian) base over an Ubuntu image\n  (stdlib-only sidecar, smallest official py3.12 runtime, smaller CVE surface).","tree":{"sha":"939ee9a0947dd15255e7a5fbdaba413f92fbae97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/939ee9a0947dd15255e7a5fbdaba413f92fbae97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/ed812945174bede360c186a7a3fff8131dbab429","verification":{"payload":"tree 939ee9a0947dd15255e7a5fbdaba413f92fbae97\nparent 688330f319c168f2a36eca39b7a3b54232f93031\nauthor shmufeld <97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com> 1782371953 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782371953 +0300\n\nstate-mirror (1/4): scaffold + foundations (#375)\n\n* state-mirror (1/4): component scaffold + foundation modules\n\nFirst slice of the StateMirror sidecar, split out of #373 for reviewability.\nNet-new, consumer-agnostic component under ufm-state-mirror/.\n\nThis PR lands the packaging/CI/docs scaffold and the dependency-free\nfoundation modules only:\n- packaging: VERSION, build/Dockerfile, build/docker_build.sh, .dockerignore,\n  pyproject (ruff/pytest config), requirements, BUILD.md, README, and the\n  example classifier.\n- CI: .github/workflows/state-mirror-ci.yml (ruff + pytest + docker build,\n  scoped to ufm-state-mirror/**).\n- engine foundations: wire (on-the-wire body+meta + integrity verify),\n  classifier (YAML schema/validation), redis_errors / k8s_errors (reason\n  taxonomies), logconfig.\n\nStorage backends, handlers, and the runtime loop follow in PRs 2-4.\nTests for these modules pass; ruff clean.\n\n* state-mirror (1/4): address review feedback\n\n- classifier: strict boolean coercion for `recursive` (a quoted \"false\" no\n  longer becomes True); reject duplicate/nested keyspaces (a redis_key under a\n  directory redis_key_prefix, or nested prefixes) and report all uniqueness\n  problems in one aggregated error instead of failing on the first; move the\n  PyYAML import to the module head.\n- redis_errors: classify redis-py exception classes via a name->reason map\n  walked over the MRO (subclass wins over base) instead of an if-chain.\n- wire / logconfig: clearer variable names (d->data, root->root_logger).\n- example classifier: note it is illustrative, not the authoritative file set\n  (which ships in the consumer repo).\n- tests: cover strict bool, keyspace overlap/nesting, and aggregated errors.\n\n* ufm-state-mirror/state_mirror/classifier.py\n\nformatting\n\n* formatting\n\n* state-mirror (1/4): address PR #375 review feedback\n\n- wire: check `body is None` before the format-version guard in verify_body so\n  a missing body reports the correct error; keep the pre-fetch format guard in\n  read_and_verify via a shared _ensure_supported_format() helper (so a too-new\n  format is still refused without fetching a possibly large body). Adds\n  regression tests for both paths.\n- wire: document the distinct roles of Meta.format_version (wire layout,\n  enforced on read) vs schema_version (reserved content-schema marker).\n- Dockerfile: justify the python:3.12-slim (Debian) base over an Ubuntu image\n  (stdlib-only sidecar, smallest official py3.12 runtime, smaller CVE surface).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPNZxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOI8QAA+GAFkIlSQMA/J18jkp0q/n\n/NARj97Hr59Z7StnfR/AJnzvvP1nCjiRjVlpR7kir2JjA23ZModUQKzhFQKaArb5\n59pSNO7ZXXId5hD/Lf6EYMxIAbanZvwHAakwXh9UUZ4X5X2pzw9wF2igf1Uan1T8\n7OhIl1zrvZmlvLjpPNW6l0V50+nB1t9FBK2GXqR75Ssxy9mwfHoGHEjfM29r6zRa\nv+RsO7N/b2GhevgJEi6kGAVqyp06065GsYg5BfZU3eZhGc8we6iCRpwuxOocBjrY\nOX+hbXUOz6q1h5tFPyXQgoD4QG4N8DluFvwkADmVl43Rx3eI75cNZs4qhyjyIHPe\nEWTeFLu06kVyh5addpjeZeNZYgMab6JCbKZhF12QtnpBqTdZdVL9KN0MdEvHNR5p\n9X3MedkF9xoihLYiRF4VgOi0+SkF6j1itAO5H42G4R4CXLn4LqLiiVwuNJV9SlZx\nJOrkEAV1mcP/tTpF6kWopKm4g2fuycDIYbpNSKmGjQYOAkYOGJuGPwQMCAlQ+grz\nDZJS4pmbIIL6m5LSD/PUXyO+80IOZfDdywYkm50HVycS8CNe3agYEzUlUWvLL4wT\ntki7WNuwZt0b8XpB0/GWwZzcW+q7H1OVKcrl144VYPmN8mL4HeUTRT7rGKP8DFEQ\nEuH5rK05J+ErDXGUHPHj\n=6suQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-25T07:19:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-