sers/shmufeld/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shmufeld","id":97442151,"login":"shmufeld","node_id":"U_kgDOBc7ZZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/846e02782d0c2e017ccfe525b98c01a7bfefcbd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-30T06:28:01Z","email":"97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com","name":"shmufeld"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-30T06:28:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ufm-plugins Helm: ClusterIP Service for in-cluster plugin DNS (4919133) (#363)\n\n* ufm-plugins Helm: ClusterIP Service for in-cluster plugin DNS (4919133)\n\nBackground\n- With hostNetwork removed, UFM must reach plugins using the host in\n  plugins.yaml (default FQDN: {ufmFullname}-plugin-{name}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local).\n  That name only resolves if a matching Kubernetes Service exists.\n\nChart\n- Add templates/plugin-service.yaml: one ClusterIP Service per plugin when\n  port and/or ports is set; selector matches the plugin Deployment; expose\n  the primary port plus any extra ports (no duplicate Service port if listed twice).\n\nDocumentation\n- README: state that the chart creates the Service; testing/CI pointers;\n  link TEST_PLAN_SERVICE.md for manual and negative test scenarios.\n\nCI\n- Add ci-values-service.yaml (8080 + extra 8443) to exercise multi-port Services.\n- helm-template-ci.yml: render and assert single Service, ClusterIP, expected\n  plugins.yaml host, and targetPort 8080/8443 within the Service manifest.\n- ci-values.yaml: comment references ci-values-service.yaml.\n\nMade-with: Cursor\n\n* issue:123456 Add plugin watchdog contract to helm chart (#362)\n\nWhat\nImplement the plugin-side watchdog contract so the UFM watchdog operator\ncan discover, monitor, and manage plugin pods. This includes opt-in\nlabels, restart threshold and time-window annotations, per-plugin\nunhealthy-node exclusion, and chart-level / per-plugin configuration.\n\nHow\n- Add watchdog values (enabled, restartThreshold, timeWindowSeconds) to\n  values.yaml with chart-level defaults and per-plugin override support.\n- Add watchdog schema validation to values.schema.json.\n- Emit watchdog labels (ufm.nvidia.com/watchdog-scope, app.kubernetes.io/component,\n  plugin-name) and annotations (restart-threshold, time-window-seconds)\n  on plugin pods when watchdog is enabled.\n- Inject per-plugin nodeAffinity to exclude nodes marked unhealthy for\n  that specific plugin (ufm.nvidia.com/<plugin-name>-unhealthy=true).\n- Update NOTES.txt to show watchdog status after deploy.\n- Document watchdog integration in README.md.\n- Add push trigger to GitHub Actions CI workflow.\n\nTesting\n- helm lint passes with all 7 CI value files.\n- helm template renders correctly for: single plugin with watchdog,\n  empty plugins, watchdog disabled, multiple plugins (each with own\n  unhealthy-label exclusion), per-plugin watchdog disable, user-provided\n  affinity merged with watchdog nodeAffinity, and log-streamer example\n  with per-plugin overrides.\n\n* Add .nspect-allowlist.toml for nspect OSS scanning (#364)\n\n* issue:4943950 Helm chart: enable incremental single-plugin upgrades (#365)\n\n* issue:4943950 Helm chart: enable incremental single-plugin upgrades\n\nRestructure the UFM plugin Helm chart so users can deploy, upgrade,\nor disable individual plugins without affecting the rest of the release.\n\n* Consolidate 8 CI values files into 3 (remove 5 redundant files)\n\nMerge multi-plugin, per-plugin-disable, affinity, strategy-rolling,\nand health-scripts scenarios into one comprehensive CI values file.\nWatchdog-disabled test now uses --set override on the baseline file.\nAll 30 CI assertions pass.\n\n* ufm-plugins Helm: ClusterIP Service for in-cluster plugin DNS (4919133)\n\nBackground\n- With hostNetwork removed, UFM must reach plugins using the host in\n  plugins.yaml (default FQDN: {ufmFullname}-plugin-{name}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local).\n  That name only resolves if a matching Kubernetes Service exists.\n\nChart\n- Add templates/plugin-service.yaml: one ClusterIP Service per plugin when\n  port and/or ports is set; selector matches the plugin Deployment; expose\n  the primary port plus any extra ports (no duplicate Service port if listed twice).\n\nDocumentation\n- README: state that the chart creates the Service; testing/CI pointers;\n  link TEST_PLAN_SERVICE.md for manual and negative test scenarios.\n\nCI\n- Add ci-values-service.yaml (8080 + extra 8443) to exercise multi-port Services.\n- helm-template-ci.yml: render and assert single Service, ClusterIP, expected\n  plugins.yaml host, and targetPort 8080/8443 within the Service manifest.\n- ci-values.yaml: comment references ci-values-service.yaml.\n\nMade-with: Cursor\n\n* fix(plugins-chart): render ClusterIP Service from plugins.entries\n\nplugin-service.yaml previously iterated plugins.items while Deployments and ConfigMaps use plugins.entries, so ClusterIP Services were not created for normal values files.\n\n- Align Service template with the same entries loop, enabled flag, and port/ports handling as Deployments.\n- Update ci-values-service.yaml to use plugins.entries and namespaceSearchList: [] for deterministic namespace in CI.\n\nTesting: helm lint with ci-values.yaml, ci-values-service.yaml, and ci-values-empty-plugins.yaml; helm template for ci-values-service.yaml matching workflow checks (single Service, type ClusterIP, plugins.yaml host aligned with Service name, targetPorts 8080 and 8443). Cluster smoke on ufm-enterprise: separate plugins ConfigMap, nginx plugin with runInitContainer false and port 80; Service ufm-ufm-enterprise-plugin-helm-smoke had ready endpoints; in-cluster curl to the Service FQDN returned HTTP 200.\nMade-with: Cursor\n\n* fix(ufm-plugin-helm): README dedupe, primary port name, Service labels,\nDeployment port dedup, remove redundant\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: boazhaim <160493207+boazhaim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: shahar spormas <sspormas@nvidia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4dcd0ea47fb1ee009bf19de4ea96638f18387977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/4dcd0ea47fb1ee009bf19de4ea96638f18387977"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/846e02782d0c2e017ccfe525b98c01a7bfefcbd6","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dcd0ea47fb1ee009bf19de4ea96638f18387977\nparent 1eff35762936cf219583ea3638597a5553b4cd68\nauthor shmufeld <97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com> 1774852081 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774852081 +0300\n\nufm-plugins Helm: ClusterIP Service for in-cluster plugin DNS (4919133) (#363)\n\n* ufm-plugins Helm: ClusterIP Service for in-cluster plugin DNS (4919133)\n\nBackground\n- With hostNetwork removed, UFM must reach plugins using the host in\n  plugins.yaml (default FQDN: {ufmFullname}-plugin-{name}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local).\n  That name only resolves if a matching Kubernetes Service exists.\n\nChart\n- Add templates/plugin-service.yaml: one ClusterIP Service per plugin when\n  port and/or ports is set; selector matches the plugin Deployment; expose\n  the primary port plus any extra ports (no duplicate Service port if listed twice).\n\nDocumentation\n- README: state that the chart creates the Service; testing/CI pointers;\n  link TEST_PLAN_SERVICE.md for manual and negative test scenarios.\n\nCI\n- Add ci-values-service.yaml (8080 + extra 8443) to exercise multi-port Services.\n- helm-template-ci.yml: render and assert single Service, ClusterIP, expected\n  plugins.yaml host, and targetPort 8080/8443 within the Service manifest.\n- ci-values.yaml: comment references ci-values-service.yaml.\n\nMade-with: Cursor\n\n* issue:123456 Add plugin watchdog contract to helm chart (#362)\n\nWhat\nImplement the plugin-side watchdog contract so the UFM watchdog operator\ncan discover, monitor, and manage plugin pods. This includes opt-in\nlabels, restart threshold and time-window annotations, per-plugin\nunhealthy-node exclusion, and chart-level / per-plugin configuration.\n\nHow\n- Add watchdog values (enabled, restartThreshold, timeWindowSeconds) to\n  values.yaml with chart-level defaults and per-plugin override support.\n- Add watchdog schema validation to values.schema.json.\n- Emit watchdog labels (ufm.nvidia.com/watchdog-scope, app.kubernetes.io/component,\n  plugin-name) and annotations (restart-threshold, time-window-seconds)\n  on plugin pods when watchdog is enabled.\n- Inject per-plugin nodeAffinity to exclude nodes marked unhealthy for\n  that specific plugin (ufm.nvidia.com/<plugin-name>-unhealthy=true).\n- Update NOTES.txt to show watchdog status after deploy.\n- Document watchdog integration in README.md.\n- Add push trigger to GitHub Actions CI workflow.\n\nTesting\n- helm lint passes with all 7 CI value files.\n- helm template renders correctly for: single plugin with watchdog,\n  empty plugins, watchdog disabled, multiple plugins (each with own\n  unhealthy-label exclusion), per-plugin watchdog disable, user-provided\n  affinity merged with watchdog nodeAffinity, and log-streamer example\n  with per-plugin overrides.\n\n* Add .nspect-allowlist.toml for nspect OSS scanning (#364)\n\n* issue:4943950 Helm chart: enable incremental single-plugin upgrades (#365)\n\n* issue:4943950 Helm chart: enable incremental single-plugin upgrades\n\nRestructure the UFM plugin Helm chart so users can deploy, upgrade,\nor disable individual plugins without affecting the rest of the release.\n\n* Consolidate 8 CI values files into 3 (remove 5 redundant files)\n\nMerge multi-plugin, per-plugin-disable, affinity, strategy-rolling,\nand health-scripts scenarios into one comprehensive CI values file.\nWatchdog-disabled test now uses --set override on the baseline file.\nAll 30 CI assertions pass.\n\n* ufm-plugins Helm: ClusterIP Service for in-cluster plugin DNS (4919133)\n\nBackground\n- With hostNetwork removed, UFM must reach plugins using the host in\n  plugins.yaml (default FQDN: {ufmFullname}-plugin-{name}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local).\n  That name only resolves if a matching Kubernetes Service exists.\n\nChart\n- Add templates/plugin-service.yaml: one ClusterIP Service per plugin when\n  port and/or ports is set; selector matches the plugin Deployment; expose\n  the primary port plus any extra ports (no duplicate Service port if listed twice).\n\nDocumentation\n- README: state that the chart creates the Service; testing/CI pointers;\n  link TEST_PLAN_SERVICE.md for manual and negative test scenarios.\n\nCI\n- Add ci-values-service.yaml (8080 + extra 8443) to exercise multi-port Services.\n- helm-template-ci.yml: render and assert single Service, ClusterIP, expected\n  plugins.yaml host, and targetPort 8080/8443 within the Service manifest.\n- ci-values.yaml: comment references ci-values-service.yaml.\n\nMade-with: Cursor\n\n* fix(plugins-chart): render ClusterIP Service from plugins.entries\n\nplugin-service.yaml previously iterated plugins.items while Deployments and ConfigMaps use plugins.entries, so ClusterIP Services were not created for normal values files.\n\n- Align Service template with the same entries loop, enabled flag, and port/ports handling as Deployments.\n- Update ci-values-service.yaml to use plugins.entries and namespaceSearchList: [] for deterministic namespace in CI.\n\nTesting: helm lint with ci-values.yaml, ci-values-service.yaml, and ci-values-empty-plugins.yaml; helm template for ci-values-service.yaml matching workflow checks (single Service, type ClusterIP, plugins.yaml host aligned with Service name, targetPorts 8080 and 8443). Cluster smoke on ufm-enterprise: separate plugins ConfigMap, nginx plugin with runInitContainer false and port 80; Service ufm-ufm-enterprise-plugin-helm-smoke had ready endpoints; in-cluster curl to the Service FQDN returned HTTP 200.\nMade-with: Cursor\n\n* fix(ufm-plugin-helm): README dedupe, primary port name, Service labels,\nDeployment port dedup, remove redundant\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: boazhaim <160493207+boazhaim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: shahar spormas <sspormas@nvidia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyhfxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+8wQAH11HyDxnWIFAY2iKULoRz+c\n8/jLWSzPytRQY2Rbb2Mw6xPO272gICvUp2I0ZMR8B4cmhe1Gnmxqbdb5jbQBpyxn\nBuTLNevcoy/nVl2qz8gutWmZeCmaH45wGkD4cIcjhOFK1qgtqXGnTBOg3SoCd65t\n7B0YAeyR8SBw7mNiQTUoM+SzAOAQCwnw5z6sikkEnmGZFQs1nqBUJ4slT/9FXpQr\ne0aE/5C0WbSE7MSqryWFc1lNfpUo3j2VlS90jxXvXkxvz1pYG4cvSy/RyBFRhP2U\nEutviTSUWwIZZqQbdyyD1jM7w6Q9i13WgYQGBCYplBCIXsJo6LnDwAANneD3C7b8\ni1qxmyOi9m+7gwoQAMMPmUT4/EP7JVZ81ZECk8XvhLI58E2KCqdDO4PYriAfhojy\n1FFTc+iJOQFVFjIawisMBtFnaTTHtbea/SsQh/hw8M504T0BkrjV9byEiJwe0GlT\n5eINJpW7lmKTKud+KZkbcPce7LOg7a5FY73ipCo3dndW7dylBP4eVlaiGNF0rEkP\nr+I8fVuLG0Pdduv9E7M92JM8i8yMZrhUGLZZ8Iv9LwGYlH/bH5hWil2xczixqqBU\nVZCQorROMp0J5FTTinZ4EuuPQCr5DuLJ8/7hji/w44ILVeL4cvdOMX1OIynOTT5U\ndgPpPrDu1Ni19gvnuRGq\n=Ww6m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-30T06:28:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com