rl":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boazhaim","id":160493207,"login":"boazhaim","node_id":"U_kgDOCZDulw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boazhaim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/8feb71accccaf65126fa16264794a938244d9e40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-23T15:27:10Z","email":"160493207+boazhaim@users.noreply.github.com","name":"boazhaim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-23T15:27:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"issue:123456 Add plugin watchdog contract to helm chart (#362)\n\nWhat\nImplement the plugin-side watchdog contract so the UFM watchdog operator\ncan discover, monitor, and manage plugin pods. This includes opt-in\nlabels, restart threshold and time-window annotations, per-plugin\nunhealthy-node exclusion, and chart-level / per-plugin configuration.\n\nHow\n- Add watchdog values (enabled, restartThreshold, timeWindowSeconds) to\n  values.yaml with chart-level defaults and per-plugin override support.\n- Add watchdog schema validation to values.schema.json.\n- Emit watchdog labels (ufm.nvidia.com/watchdog-scope, app.kubernetes.io/component,\n  plugin-name) and annotations (restart-threshold, time-window-seconds)\n  on plugin pods when watchdog is enabled.\n- Inject per-plugin nodeAffinity to exclude nodes marked unhealthy for\n  that specific plugin (ufm.nvidia.com/<plugin-name>-unhealthy=true).\n- Update NOTES.txt to show watchdog status after deploy.\n- Document watchdog integration in README.md.\n- Add push trigger to GitHub Actions CI workflow.\n\nTesting\n- helm lint passes with all 7 CI value files.\n- helm template renders correctly for: single plugin with watchdog,\n  empty plugins, watchdog disabled, multiple plugins (each with own\n  unhealthy-label exclusion), per-plugin watchdog disable, user-provided\n  affinity merged with watchdog nodeAffinity, and log-streamer example\n  with per-plugin overrides.","tree":{"sha":"3f2370f1ca8ebeec85d6f3fc636a9a878d7ac7f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/3f2370f1ca8ebeec85d6f3fc636a9a878d7ac7f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/8feb71accccaf65126fa16264794a938244d9e40","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f2370f1ca8ebeec85d6f3fc636a9a878d7ac7f6\nparent 480a5c8994123d86121db23b4dd039cc886ea9bd\nauthor boazhaim <160493207+boazhaim@users.noreply.github.com> 1774279630 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774279630 +0200\n\nissue:123456 Add plugin watchdog contract to helm chart (#362)\n\nWhat\nImplement the plugin-side watchdog contract so the UFM watchdog operator\ncan discover, monitor, and manage plugin pods. This includes opt-in\nlabels, restart threshold and time-window annotations, per-plugin\nunhealthy-node exclusion, and chart-level / per-plugin configuration.\n\nHow\n- Add watchdog values (enabled, restartThreshold, timeWindowSeconds) to\n  values.yaml with chart-level defaults and per-plugin override support.\n- Add watchdog schema validation to values.schema.json.\n- Emit watchdog labels (ufm.nvidia.com/watchdog-scope, app.kubernetes.io/component,\n  plugin-name) and annotations (restart-threshold, time-window-seconds)\n  on plugin pods when watchdog is enabled.\n- Inject per-plugin nodeAffinity to exclude nodes marked unhealthy for\n  that specific plugin (ufm.nvidia.com/<plugin-name>-unhealthy=true).\n- Update NOTES.txt to show watchdog status after deploy.\n- Document watchdog integration in README.md.\n- Add push trigger to GitHub Actions CI workflow.\n\nTesting\n- helm lint passes with all 7 CI value files.\n- helm template renders correctly for: single plugin with watchdog,\n  empty plugins, watchdog disabled, multiple plugins (each with own\n  unhealthy-label exclusion), per-plugin watchdog disable, user-provided\n  affinity merged with watchdog nodeAffinity, and log-streamer example\n  with per-plugin overrides.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwVvOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPmQQABc9aClOV5PxGrviqmUpFxxZ\nzQ6of9G1EPK9oD1gkF2i1FlPmQ9nJBvgml35huvVCqLdJYTfUBPtGqpO25XxKu2I\nY5GTiSrJdSYiDeRe5Hxd9CLaq8VSwP4gpCBaEMUY4xrTbMHl9ZxpTRZV9gSiG2EH\nS6FIWvAjy1zVrhRf/ExtIajbrmx1GsiKOZGQjT1Uver1LDh8JvBCRxUK5N4EPWtv\nc5oqgsLXjNUHL4yyhlkagoLd7VwiXxF5M1wIS258czDWORykR3X1UanpcOhsEmq5\nBumR4BplpSMcq4sCv3hGswPbQJ+zXo7o/fD3W9l9OIcgwZTCEd+EfOz2sHacOiL5\nJsABnBRVWN/0ToLLebrnxu2Y9WPZ8OAGsP5bzRCCWQDGrTaz5Qrj8N/zemprQi3Z\n89ZoA/leGBdD9YKJAGp9lRkgm3Ebpyd52tfDemn4y0yk8qsxXYixraFPdUEfbfPW\nqlxGF3aO+5QC9NLh+IMYw3LYFgIyhUJqSOAdCzMsFK7GBj77YnvzTTdas00y7wHS\nnCGZiVSAlEunBflzh5ysPf53dyn3cJsfrtDDXIUkIz+CeT9GO6ov4OliZG0ihAx0\nVdlyKh8mKVTkCgrQ/GhPk5t3avC9FqVR7OXc742Lj2TUaIYsmbL66LVzK5QdovSK\nR288yJO4/U5KUns37PjN\n=w6gx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-23T15:27:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commit/8feb71accccaf65126fa16264794a938244d9e40","node_id":"C_kwDOHRI_RdoAKDhmZWI3MWFjY2NjYWY2NTEyNmZhMTYyNjQ3OTRhOTM4MjQ0ZDllNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commit/480a5c8994123d86121db23b4dd039cc886ea9bd","sha":"480a5c8994123d86121db23b4dd039cc886ea9bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/480a5c8994123d86121db23b4dd039cc886ea9bd"}],"sha":"8feb71accccaf65126fa16264794a938244d9e40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/8feb71accccaf65126fa16264794a938244d9e40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97442151?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shmufeld","id":97442151,"login":"shmufeld","node_id":"U_kgDOBc7ZZw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmufeld","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/commits/480a5c8994123d86121db23b4dd039cc886ea9bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-18T13:25:13Z","email":"97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com","name":"shmufeld"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-18T13:25:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"issue:4878670 helm template for UFM plugins (#361)\n\n* helm template for UFM plugins.\n\n* helming plugin chart as part of the CI\n\n* ufm-plugin-helm: address review findings and CI artifact copy\n\nHelm chart and CI changes:\n\n1. Health probes (High)\n   - Fix check_http/check_tcp in plugin-health-configmap: return 1 on\n     failure instead of unconditional return 0 so liveness/readiness\n     correctly fail when UFM or plugin endpoints are down.\n\n2. UFM URL for probes (High)\n   - Stop defaulting to 127.0.0.1 (plugin pod itself). Chart now\n     injects UFM_URL from in-cluster service\n     (http://{ufmFullname}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local:8000/app/ufm_version).\n   - Add values.ufmUrl for override. Health script only checks UFM when\n     UFM_URL is set.\n\n3. CI script execution (High)\n   - Invoke do_create_ufm_plugin_helm_chart.sh with ''bash'' so the step\n     does not depend on the script execute bit (avoids Permission denied).\n\n4. RDMA optional (Medium)\n   - Default rdma.resourceCount to \"0\". Add conditional in\n     plugin-deployment so RDMA limits are only set when resourceCount\n     is not \"0\", avoiding unschedulable pods for non-RDMA plugins.\n\n5. README probe keys (Medium)\n   - Document the same keys the template uses (livenessInitialDelay,\n     livenessPeriod, etc.) and add ufmUrl/rdma defaults.\n\n6. CI template coverage (Medium)\n   - Add a minimal plugin item to ci-values.yaml so helm lint/template\n     exercise plugin-deployment and plugin-health-configmap.\n\n7. Example artifact name (Low)\n   - In examples/log-streamer-config.yaml, fix comment to\n     ufm-plugin-<version>-helm.tgz to match script output.\n\nCI (ci_matrix.yaml):\n   - Build step writes chart package to /tmp/ufm-helm.\n   - pipeline_start: ensure /tmp/ufm-helm and job artifact dir exist.\n   - pipeline_stop: copy /tmp/ufm-helm/* to job artifact dir as\n     swx-jenkins (|| true so stop step does not fail).\n\n* fixing ci issue\n\n* Update ci_matrix.yaml\n\n* fix Boaz''s comments\n\n* fix Dror''s comments\n\n* ufm-plugin-helm: default liveness via health-check.sh, readiness user-defined; discover namespace at install\n\n- Restore plugin-health-configmap; use it only for default liveness.\n  Readiness has no default. Re-add healthEndpoint/healthPort and volume.\n- Discover namespace at install with Helm lookup (ConfigMap\n  {ufmFullname}-config); fallback to values.namespace / ufm-enterprise.\n- Update README and values for liveness/readiness and discovery.\n\n* add github action\n\n* Delete .ci/ci_matrix.yaml\n\nremove redundant\n\n* revert redundant\n\n* - Generic chart: install once, pass a plugins definition file (-f). README\n  and Chart.yaml present the chart as generic; no copy/customize flow.\n- Namespace discovery: scope to namespaceSearchList (get ConfigMap per\n  namespace only). No cluster-wide list; add namespaceSearchList to values.\n- Init container: add IPC_LOCK when RDMA enabled (was only on main container).\n- Main container: optional extraCapabilities; custom env (per-plugin env);\n  optional volumes and volumeMounts per plugin.\n- Resources: only emit limits when there is at least one limit (fix empty\n  limits block). Only emit requests when $res.requests is set.\n- Liveness: allow disableLivenessProbe; default liveness uses native\n  httpGet (when healthEndpoint set) or tcpSocket (when port set) instead\n  of bash script.\n- Health script: move to scripts/health-check.sh and include in ConfigMap\n  via .Files.Get for easier reading/editing; default liveness no longer\n  uses the script (native K8s probes only).\n- README: document all new options; clarify default liveness and script\n  usage.\n\n* ufm-plugins chart: review fixes and production hardening\n\nChart / packaging\n- Bump version to 0.1.0\n- Add .helmignore (exclude examples, CI values, REVIEW_QA, COMMIT_MSG from package)\n- Add templates/NOTES.txt with post-install commands (list pods, logs)\n- Add values.schema.json: require ufmFullname (minLength 1), plugins.items[].name/image/tag; catch typos at install time\n\nPlugin deployment\n- Default host: use in-cluster DNS ({ufmFullname}-plugin-{name}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local) instead of 127.0.0.1 so UFM (in another pod) can reach plugins; document Service or host override\n- Per-plugin RDMA: plugin item can set rdma: { resourceName, resourceCount } to mix RDMA and non-RDMA plugins\n- Multiple ports: optional ports: [] per plugin; containerPorts for port + ports; port remains primary for plugins.yaml\n- startupProbe: optional per-plugin startupProbe for slow-starting plugins\n- Liveness: use \"if not .disableLivenessProbe\" instead of double-negative; consistent indentation in env/liveness blocks\n- Health-scripts: mount volume and emit ConfigMap only when at least one plugin has mountHealthScripts: true (default liveness uses native httpGet/tcpSocket)\n- Resources: omit resources: block when no requests/limits (main + init container) to avoid bare key rejected by some admission controllers\n- Init container: add runInitContainer: false per plugin to skip init (for images without /init.sh)\n- Pod security: add podSecurityContext (values) for runAsNonRoot, runAsUser, seccompProfile (Pod Security Standards)\n- Add app.kubernetes.io/instance label for NOTES kubectl examples\n\nDocs\n- README: host default, podSecurityContext, runInitContainer, ports, startupProbe, per-plugin rdma, values.schema.json section, NOTES mention","tree":{"sha":"920b702fa60c5e098296f83bc152ecae01c5e37f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/trees/920b702fa60c5e098296f83bc152ecae01c5e37f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mellanox/ufm_sdk_3.0/git/commits/480a5c8994123d86121db23b4dd039cc886ea9bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 920b702fa60c5e098296f83bc152ecae01c5e37f\nparent 6dccd0ce06bada7255d10ec632a375904f3046ed\nauthor shmufeld <97442151+shmufeld@users.noreply.github.com> 1773840313 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773840313 +0200\n\nissue:4878670 helm template for UFM plugins (#361)\n\n* helm template for UFM plugins.\n\n* helming plugin chart as part of the CI\n\n* ufm-plugin-helm: address review findings and CI artifact copy\n\nHelm chart and CI changes:\n\n1. Health probes (High)\n   - Fix check_http/check_tcp in plugin-health-configmap: return 1 on\n     failure instead of unconditional return 0 so liveness/readiness\n     correctly fail when UFM or plugin endpoints are down.\n\n2. UFM URL for probes (High)\n   - Stop defaulting to 127.0.0.1 (plugin pod itself). Chart now\n     injects UFM_URL from in-cluster service\n     (http://{ufmFullname}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local:8000/app/ufm_version).\n   - Add values.ufmUrl for override. Health script only checks UFM when\n     UFM_URL is set.\n\n3. CI script execution (High)\n   - Invoke do_create_ufm_plugin_helm_chart.sh with ''bash'' so the step\n     does not depend on the script execute bit (avoids Permission denied).\n\n4. RDMA optional (Medium)\n   - Default rdma.resourceCount to \"0\". Add conditional in\n     plugin-deployment so RDMA limits are only set when resourceCount\n     is not \"0\", avoiding unschedulable pods for non-RDMA plugins.\n\n5. README probe keys (Medium)\n   - Document the same keys the template uses (livenessInitialDelay,\n     livenessPeriod, etc.) and add ufmUrl/rdma defaults.\n\n6. CI template coverage (Medium)\n   - Add a minimal plugin item to ci-values.yaml so helm lint/template\n     exercise plugin-deployment and plugin-health-configmap.\n\n7. Example artifact name (Low)\n   - In examples/log-streamer-config.yaml, fix comment to\n     ufm-plugin-<version>-helm.tgz to match script output.\n\nCI (ci_matrix.yaml):\n   - Build step writes chart package to /tmp/ufm-helm.\n   - pipeline_start: ensure /tmp/ufm-helm and job artifact dir exist.\n   - pipeline_stop: copy /tmp/ufm-helm/* to job artifact dir as\n     swx-jenkins (|| true so stop step does not fail).\n\n* fixing ci issue\n\n* Update ci_matrix.yaml\n\n* fix Boaz''s comments\n\n* fix Dror''s comments\n\n* ufm-plugin-helm: default liveness via health-check.sh, readiness user-defined; discover namespace at install\n\n- Restore plugin-health-configmap; use it only for default liveness.\n  Readiness has no default. Re-add healthEndpoint/healthPort and volume.\n- Discover namespace at install with Helm lookup (ConfigMap\n  {ufmFullname}-config); fallback to values.namespace / ufm-enterprise.\n- Update README and values for liveness/readiness and discovery.\n\n* add github action\n\n* Delete .ci/ci_matrix.yaml\n\nremove redundant\n\n* revert redundant\n\n* - Generic chart: install once, pass a plugins definition file (-f). README\n  and Chart.yaml present the chart as generic; no copy/customize flow.\n- Namespace discovery: scope to namespaceSearchList (get ConfigMap per\n  namespace only). No cluster-wide list; add namespaceSearchList to values.\n- Init container: add IPC_LOCK when RDMA enabled (was only on main container).\n- Main container: optional extraCapabilities; custom env (per-plugin env);\n  optional volumes and volumeMounts per plugin.\n- Resources: only emit limits when there is at least one limit (fix empty\n  limits block). Only emit requests when $res.requests is set.\n- Liveness: allow disableLivenessProbe; default liveness uses native\n  httpGet (when healthEndpoint set) or tcpSocket (when port set) instead\n  of bash script.\n- Health script: move to scripts/health-check.sh and include in ConfigMap\n  via .Files.Get for easier reading/editing; default liveness no longer\n  uses the script (native K8s probes only).\n- README: document all new options; clarify default liveness and script\n  usage.\n\n* ufm-plugins chart: review fixes and production hardening\n\nChart / packaging\n- Bump version to 0.1.0\n- Add .helmignore (exclude examples, CI values, REVIEW_QA, COMMIT_MSG from package)\n- Add templates/NOTES.txt with post-install commands (list pods, logs)\n- Add values.schema.json: require ufmFullname (minLength 1), plugins.items[].name/image/tag; catch typos at install time\n\nPlugin deployment\n- Default host: use in-cluster DNS ({ufmFullname}-plugin-{name}.{namespace}.svc.cluster.local) instead of 127.0.0.1 so UFM (in another pod) can reach plugins; document Service or host override\n- Per-plugin RDMA: plugin item can set rdma: { resourceName, resourceCount } to mix RDMA and non-RDMA plugins\n- Multiple ports: optional ports: [] per plugin; containerPorts for port + ports; port remains primary for plugins.yaml\n- startupProbe: optional per-plugin startupProbe for slow-starting plugins\n- Liveness: use \"if not .disableLivenessProbe\" instead of double-negative; consistent indentation in env/liveness blocks\n- Health-scripts: mount volume and emit ConfigMap only when at least one plugin has mountHealthScripts: true (default liveness uses native httpGet/tcpSocket)\n- Resources: omit resources: block when no requests/limits (main + init container) to avoid bare key rejected by some admission controllers\n- Init container: add runInitContainer: false per plugin to skip init (for images without /init.sh)\n- Pod security: add podSecurityContext (values) for runAsNonRoot, runAsUser, seccompProfile (Pod Security Standards)\n- Add app.kubernetes.io/instance label for NOTES kubectl examples\n\nDocs\n- README: host default, podSecurityContext, runInitContainer, ports, startupProbe, per-plugin rdma, values.schema.json section, NOTES mention","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpuqe5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxpkQABNuPLIiyYgylYGo5eMHgJij\n+LNYKYjUHVHPCpJ6c6D+hRJevnL8xmDdSLv/GRvdr0r9ZPznX6oQmaHMFSOCgaRf\nxHjkyYkvJmYrmHtNLOvrgcNKGapBsvDGx24h1hRBawro0hPZg1xC0L61r9YtIY8X\nPHLxUuvBNLiPgrkTqyf1H+1jHXyKoK462G8i8CeMpNBRnoqiamx2T+gWUSns/6eK\n4UbiyfeQ5bdP+CMwcvqtX7YEhKL5eQEp8B6YNK/2Q